From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: raise the time limit for the hardest MIP cases on
 slow CI runners

Upstream-Status: To upstream [no riscv64 CI leg upstream has to validate this against; raises the already-acknowledged "generous" limit further for genuinely slower hardware]

CASES' comment already says "Time limits are generous to avoid false
failures on slow CI runners", but 2000s still isn't enough on this
fleet's riscv64 hardware for six of the harder MIPLIB instances
(mzzv11, pk1, mas76, eil33-2, markshare_4_0, neos-860300): CBC hits
"Result - Stopped on time limit" before proving optimality, in both
test_solve (1 thread) and test_solve_parallel (3 threads):

  FAILED tests/test_solve.py::test_solve[generic-mzzv11.mps.gz--21718.0-2000]
  FAILED tests/test_solve.py::test_solve[generic-neos-860300.mps.gz-3201.0-2000]
  FAILED tests/test_solve.py::test_solve_parallel[generic-pk1.mps.gz-11.0-2000]
  FAILED tests/test_solve.py::test_solve_parallel[generic-mas76.mps.gz-40005.054142-2000]
  FAILED tests/test_solve.py::test_solve_parallel[generic-eil33-2.mps.gz-934.007916-2000]
  FAILED tests/test_solve.py::test_solve_parallel[generic-markshare_4_0.mps.gz-1.0-2000]

Every other case already passes comfortably inside 2000s; raise just
these six to 4000s (subprocess timeout follows automatically, since it
is derived as time_limit + 120). The fastest CPUs this project's own CI
runs on are several times quicker per core than this fleet's riscv64
runners for exactly this kind of branch-and-bound-heavy workload, so
this isn't a defect in the port, only a harder cutoff than upstream's
own runners ever needed to hit.

diff --git a/tests/test_solve.py b/tests/test_solve.py
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/tests/test_solve.py
+++ b/tests/test_solve.py
@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@ CASES = [
     ("air04.mps.gz",                    56137.0,          2000),
     ("air05.mps.gz",                    26374.0,          2000),
     ("nw04.mps.gz",                     16862.0,          2000),
-    ("mzzv11.mps.gz",                   -21718.0,         2000),
+    ("mzzv11.mps.gz",                   -21718.0,         4000),
     ("trd445c.mps.gz",                  -153419.078836,   2000),
     ("nursesched-sprint02.mps.gz",      58.0,             2000),
     ("stein45.mps.gz",                  30.0,             2000),
@@ -51,21 +51,21 @@ CASES = [
     ("j3050_8.mps.gz",                  1.0,              2000),
     ("qiu.mps.gz",                      -132.873136947,   2000),
     ("gesa2-o.mps.gz",                  25779856.3717,    2000),
-    ("pk1.mps.gz",                      11.0,             2000),
-    ("mas76.mps.gz",                    40005.054142,     2000),
+    ("pk1.mps.gz",                      11.0,             4000),
+    ("mas76.mps.gz",                    40005.054142,     4000),
     ("app1-1.mps.gz",                  -3.0,             2000),
-    ("eil33-2.mps.gz",                  934.007916,       2000),
+    ("eil33-2.mps.gz",                  934.007916,       4000),
     ("fiber.mps.gz",                    405935.18,        2000),
